[:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 – 29 September 2000"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/744"} "Olympic Stadium, Olympic Park, Sydney, New South Wales"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/65440"} "40 from 29 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "It was a foregone conclusion that a Kenyan would win, so dominant were they by now in the steeplechase. Their three runners included 1997 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/88165"} "Wilson Boit Kipketer"] " the runner-up in that race, and world record holder, " [:a {:href "/athletes/88157"} "Bernard Barmasai"] ", and 1998 World Junior Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/88168"} "Reuben Kosgei"] ", who had been initially entered by the name of Reuben Seroney. The pace in the final was funereal, with 1998 European Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/82612"} "Damian Kallabis"] " (GER) falling at the first hurdle in the mass pack. Kosgei took the lead at 2,000 metres and was never headed, although Boit Kipketer pulled to his shoulder near the finish. They bumped slightly on the run-in and Kosgei edged ahead at the line."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2383"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88168"} "Reuben Kosgei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KEN.png"}] "KEN"]] [:td {} "8:23.17 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "8:21.43 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2380"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88165"} "Wilson Boit Kipketer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; ve